From 678407c49c0bba72cb92399315ebfd2d130549cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Barbaros=20G=C3=B6ren?=
 <20913374+7tg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:08:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: the PS5's keyboard in the game, touchpad + triangle

A player with only a DualSense had no way to type: a game's text field
(a login, a name) took a USB keyboard or nothing. Holding the touchpad
and pressing triangle now opens the system keyboard (libSceImeDialog)
over the game, for the pad's user. What the player confirms is typed as
the keys a US keyboard sends for it (src/pw_text_keys.c): Shift around a
capital or a shifted symbol, one key event a frame, so a press and its
release never share a frame; through the USB keyboard's path, so Wine's
messages and DirectInput's scan codes both see it. Characters a US
keyboard has no key for are skipped and counted. Enter is not added.

From the chord's press until triangle is released, triangle is kept
from the game (XInput Y and bindings; src/pw_ime_chord.c). The module
is loaded early with the keyboard and mouse modules; CommonDialog, which
the payload SDK omits, links through a facade as the store launcher's
does. The log has the dialog's results and key counts, never the text.
